    "content2": {
        "content": "Themes help maintain consistent styling across your app (colors, fonts, shapes). This guide covers how to use Flutter's theming system effectively.",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "typeOf": "Text"
    },
    "content3": {
        "content": "📌 What is a Theme?",
        "type": "sub-heading",
        "typeOf": "Text"
    },
    "content4": {
        "content": "A theme defines the visual design of your app, including:\nTableColors (primary, accent, background)\nTableText styles (headlines, body text)\nTableShapes (buttons, cards)\nThink of it like a \"design rulebook\" for your app.",
        "type": "points",
        "typeOf": "List"
    },
    "content5": {
        "content": {
            "index": 1,
            "question": "What is the PRIMARY purpose of using themes in Flutter?",
            "option": [
                "To reduce app size",
                "To maintain consistent styling across the app",
                "To improve app performance",
                "To enable platform-specific features"
            ],
            "ans": "To maintain consistent styling across the app",
            "ansSuggesstion": "Themes ensure visual consistency in colors, fonts, and shapes throughout the app."
        },
        "type": "break",
        "typeOf": "mcq-break"
    },
